{{Acquisition|*Secondary Fortifier can be obtained from [[Ascension]]'s optional [[Sisters of Parvos (Ascension Mode)|Sister of Parvos]], summoned by acquiring 3 Sister Beacons during the elevator ride. 
*Purchaseable from [[Ordis]] in the [[Drifter's Camp]] for 10 {{Resource|Vestigial Motes}}, for a total of 210 for max rank.
*Possible reward from [[Bounty#Deepmines Bounties|Deepmines Bounties]] from [[Nightcap]].
*Purchaseable from [[Nightcap]] in [[Fortuna]] at '''Rank 3: Seeker''', for 10 {{Resource|Fergolyte}} each, with a total of 210 for max rank.}}

==Notes==
*{{D|Overguard}} cap is '''15,000''' at all ranks.
*[[DoT]]s will also steal {{D|Overguard}}, [[AoE]] DoTs (e.g. {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Gas}}) and weapons (e.g. {{Weapon|Aegrit}}) are great at improving crowd control over [[Eximus]].
*The {{D|Overguard}} steal effect can be "[[Heat Inherit|inherited]]" if the first source of {{D|Heat}} status applied to an enemy was from a secondary with this Arcane active.
**Extra damage to {{D|Overguard}} is not inheritable and is dynamically applied, so the effect is lost entirely after depleting the {{D|Overguard}} from an enemy.
*Since {{D|Overguard}}'s immunity period is 0.5 seconds, any secondary with a firing rate >2.0 can maintain functional immortality as long as you can keep firing and there's overguard to steal.
**This can be accomplished with {{Weapon|Grimoire}} and {{M|Lethal Torrent}} by providing a 2.4 Fire Rate with its infinite ammo.

==Bugs==
*Damage dealt during {{WF|Hildryn}}'s {{A|Aegis Storm}} can steal {{D|Overguard}} at the end of the ability.
*{{WF|Mirage}}'s {{A|Hall of Mirrors}} ability doesn't activate Secondary Fortifier, but seems to take priority making you receive zero {{D|Overguard}} whilst the ability is active.
*Damage dealt by [[Aim Glide]] and [[Bullet Jump]] can steal {{D|Overguard}}.
*Damage dealt by dying {{E|Arbitration Shield Drone}}s can steal {{D|Overguard}}.

